Subject: dialog: each closing dialog keeps its own timer, so a close never swallows the next

What: the dialog stack tracks closing dialogs in a map of per-id timers instead of one shared timer and lock; close() picks the top dialog that is not already closing, and show() clears the timers of the dialogs it replaces.
Why: with one lock, any close() during another dialog's 100 ms exit returned without closing anything, so a stacked dialog (the folder picker on the create-project dialog) could not be closed right after another; with one timer, a push or show during that exit cancelled the closing dialog's disposal and left it in the stack.

